# Names only. Copy to .env (never committed, never served) and fill in. Do not put real values in this file.
# Discord application (OAuth2: scopes identify + guilds; the redirect URI below must be registered with it)
DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=
DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=
DISCORD_REDIRECT_URI=
# The Raidsmith bot's token (Phase 7, Discord role mapping). The bot is silent and HTTP-only (invite scope bot, permissions 0): the Worker only reads a server's roles and one member's roles with it.
# Leave it empty and the role mapping is off (nothing else changes). Never commit it; set it as a secret on the platform.
DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=
# Comma-separated Discord user ids allowed to create a guild. Leave it empty to let any signed-in Discord user who owns or administers
# (Administrator or Manage Server) a Discord server create a guild for it. Set it to limit creation to those ids (the pilot).
GUILD_CREATOR_ALLOWLIST=
# Warcraft Logs client credentials (Phase 3)
WCL_CLIENT_ID=
WCL_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Battle.net API client (Phase 5; create it at develop.battle.net). The redirect URI below must be registered with it, e.g. http://localhost:8787/auth/bnet/callback
BNET_CLIENT_ID=
BNET_CLIENT_SECRET=
BNET_REDIRECT_URI=
# Block tombstones (Raidsmith blocks): the secret that hashes the keys of a blocked person (Discord id, Battle.net id, Battle.net-proven characters) so a block survives Delete my data.
# 16+ characters, e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`. Set it as a Worker secret. Unset: blocks still apply, flagged, and the daily job adds the tombstones once it is set.
TOMBSTONE_KEY=
# The version of TOMBSTONE_KEY (a whole number from 1; empty = 1). Raise it when rotating.
TOMBSTONE_KEY_VERSION=
# Retired keys that stored tombstones still use, `<version>:<secret>,<version>:<secret>`.
TOMBSTONE_OLD_KEYS=
# Dev only: 1 turns on the Guild Master's "View as" role switcher, on 127.0.0.1 / localhost only (see the README). Never set it on a deployed Worker.
DEV_VIEW_AS=
